\title{04 · Formal category theory (stage 2, \ref{ms-0005})}
\taxon{Chapter}
\meta{origin}{design/04-formal-theory.md}
\meta{layer}{human}
\tag{chapter}

\p{Formal category theory is developed once, for augmented virtual ∞-equipments, using only the VDC∞ interface. Instances: \code{Cat = Mod(Mat Set)} (discrete), \code{Mod(Mat Kan)} (∞-categories and profunctors, \ref{ms-0006}), \code{Mod(Span S)} (internal, \ref{ms-0005}/\ref{ms-0006}), and \code{Mod(P)} for any equipment \code{P} (→ \ref{at-ft-0003}). This is the layer where "not written down" is the point (→ \ref{dec-ch-0006}): definitions follow Koudenburg's augmented framework and Cruttwell–Shulman, transported to VDC∞s; the acceptance tests are the discrete and non-virtual comparisons.}
